{
 "_doc": "Fingering data. tables[kind] maps a key to an array of options (first = standard). rec and recGerman are keyed by written pitch minus the instrument's base (soprano and alto recorder share one table; recGerman holds only the notes where the German system differs); every other table is keyed by written MIDI pitch. overrides[instId][pitch] replaces the kind table's entry for that instrument; an empty array there means that instrument has no sourced fingering for the pitch (listed in fingering-gaps.json). meta[kind] = {sources: [{title, url, accessed}], reviewed}; reviewed null = draft. Pitches with no published fingering have no entry and are listed in fingering-gaps.json. Entries come from published charts only. LAYOUT[kind] = main holes/keys of the vertical column: [dx, dyTop, size(px), double?] relative to the chart centre x and chart top (px at 1x). Values in an option's 'h' array follow that order: 1 = closed/pressed, 0 = open, 0.5 = half-hole (or, for recorder double holes, only the larger hole closed). Xaphoon order: top hole, thumb, holes 3-9. SATS[kind] = satellite keys: id -> [centreX, centreY, cluster]. SHAPE[cluster] = [w,h] in the full key map (compact mode draws 5px dots). Option objects: {h, x: [satellite ids pressed], n: name, p: penalty used by the fingering chooser (0 = standard)}. FINGER maps satellite ids to the finger that operates them (used to penalise same-finger slides).",
